---
import MarketingLayout from '@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title={`Carbon Methodology — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description="Public, versioned, peer-review-ready carbon methodology behind every figure produced by MailLighter Enterprise."
>
  <section class="doc-hero">
    <div class="doc-hero-inner">
      <span class="doc-eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-base">Methodology</span><span class="eyebrow-accent">v1.0</span></span>
      <h1 class="doc-title"><span class="doc-title-green">Carbon</span> Methodology</h1>
      <p class="doc-sub">Public, versioned, peer-review-ready. The complete approach behind every figure produced by MailLighter Enterprise.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-body">
    <div class="doc-section">
      <div class="md-downloads">
        <a href="#download-coming-soon" class="btn-primary">
          <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M7.5 2v8M5 7l2.5 3 2.5-3M2 12h11"/></svg>
          Download methodology v1.0 (PDF)
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="md-download-note"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>PDFs will be published alongside the public launch. The HTML synthesis below covers the same scope.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>1. Foreword</h2>
      <p>This methodology underpins every figure published by MailLighter, from the unitary CO₂ avoided per cleanup on the public landing to the aggregated CSRD-ready report in MailLighter Enterprise. It is meant to be public, conservative, and reviewable by any third party.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>2. Scope of the methodology</h2>
      <p>The methodology covers carbon emissions avoided by reducing the size of outgoing emails composed in Microsoft Outlook with MailLighter. It excludes scope-3 hardware footprint and end-user device energy, which are already accounted for elsewhere in standard sustainability frameworks.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>3. Reference frameworks</h2>
      <p>Aligned with the GHG Protocol Corporate Standard, ADEME Base Empreinte 2025 emission factors for digital services, and ESRS E1 disclosure requirements for sustainability reporting.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>4. Measurement architecture</h2>
      <p>Cleanup events are measured locally inside Outlook. Only when an email is actually sent are the corresponding metrics transmitted to the Enterprise backend. Five fields per cleanup, no email content. See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for the exact list.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>5. Components of avoided emissions</h2>
      <p>Three categories: data transmission (network), data storage (per recipient × retention period), and replication for backup. Each component uses ADEME 2025 emission factors and is summed at the unitary cleanup level.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>6. Calculation formula</h2>
      <p><code>CO₂ (g) = bytes saved (MB) × recipients × (0.06 + 0.02 × storage_months + 0.01)</code> — i.e. <code>bytes × recipients × 0.55</code> for the 24-month default retention used on the landing page. Each constant is sourced from a published emission factor; see the PDF for the per-coefficient bibliography.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>7. Assumptions and methodological safeguards</h2>
      <p>Conservative defaults: 24-month email retention, no double-counting between cleanups on the same draft, exclusion of unsent drafts. When in doubt, the methodology under-reports rather than over-reports.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>8. Reporting and deliverables</h2>
      <p>For Enterprise customers: a real-time dashboard, an annual PDF aligned with ESRS E1, and a CSV export for internal audit. All numbers can be reproduced by recomputing the formula from the raw counters.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>9. Governance and versioning</h2>
      <p>The methodology is versioned (current: v1.0). Material changes trigger a new version with public changelog. Minor clarifications keep the same version. The Enterprise backend stamps each datapoint with the methodology version in effect at recording time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>10. Known limitations</h2>
      <p>The model does not yet account for variations in datacenter PUE per region, nor for the carbon cost of email indexing on the receiver side. Those are explicitly out of scope for v1.0 and tracked as candidates for v2.0.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>11. Appendices</h2>
      <p>The PDF version includes: full bibliography, sample calculations, cross-references with ADEME and GHG Protocol, glossary of terms, and an audit checklist for internal sustainability reviews.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>Version history</h2>
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Version</th><th>Date</th><th>Changes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1.0</td><td>May 2026</td><td>Initial publication</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-section">
      <h2>Contact for methodology questions</h2>
      <p>For methodological questions, peer review proposals, or audit requests:<br><a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.enterprise.email}`}><strong>{siteConfig.enterprise.email}</strong></a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  @keyframes fadeUp { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }

  .doc-hero { position: relative; padding: 100px 52px 56px; text-align: center; overflow: hidden; }
  .doc-hero::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; z-index: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 50% at 30% 0%, rgba(21,100,192,0.10), transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 50% at 80% 20%, rgba(74,162,81,0.08), transparent 60%);
  }
  :global(.dark) .doc-hero::before {
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 50% at 30% 0%, rgba(21,100,192,0.18), transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 50% at 80% 20%, rgba(74,162,81,0.14), transparent 60%);
  }
  .doc-hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .doc-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
    background: var(--ml-blue-pale); color: var(--ml-blue);
    font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 6px 4px 12px; border-radius: 999px;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 16px;
    animation: fadeUp 0.6s ease-out both;
  }
  .doc-eyebrow .eyebrow-base { padding-right: 4px; }
  .doc-eyebrow .eyebrow-accent {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
    background: var(--ml-green-pale); color: var(--ml-green-dark);
    padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.68rem;
  }
  :global(.dark) .doc-eyebrow .eyebrow-accent { color: var(--ml-green); }
  .doc-title { font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 16px; animation: fadeUp 0.6s ease-out 0.1s both; }
  .doc-title-green { color: var(--ml-green); }
  .doc-sub { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--ml-ink-soft); line-height: 1.75; max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto; animation: fadeUp 0.6s ease-out 0.2s both; }

  .doc-body { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 52px 100px; }
  .doc-section { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .doc-section h2 {
    position: relative;
    font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 14px;
    padding-bottom: 10px; padding-left: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .doc-section h2::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 4px; bottom: 14px;
    width: 3px; border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--ml-blue), var(--ml-green));
  }
  .doc-section p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ml-ink-soft); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .doc-section a { color: var(--ml-blue); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; }
  .doc-section a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .doc-section code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.86rem; background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--ml-ink);
  }

  .md-downloads { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .md-download-note { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ml-ink-mute); font-style: italic; text-align: center; justify-content: center; width: 100%; }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
    background: var(--ml-blue); color: white;
    padding: 13px 26px; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none; box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(21,100,192,0.3);
    transition: background 0.22s, transform 0.22s, box-shadow 0.22s;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--ml-blue-dark); transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(21,100,192,0.35); }
  .doc-section .btn-primary { color: white; text-decoration: none; }

  .md-table {
    width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .md-table th, .md-table td {
    padding: 10px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    text-align: left; color: var(--ml-ink-soft);
  }
  .md-table th {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--ml-blue-pale), var(--color-surface));
    color: var(--ml-ink); font-weight: 700;
  }
  .md-table tbody tr { transition: background 0.18s; }
  .md-table tbody tr:hover { background: rgba(21,100,192,0.04); }
  :global(.dark) .md-table tbody tr:hover { background: rgba(21,100,192,0.10); }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .doc-hero { padding: 80px 24px 40px; }
    .doc-body { padding: 0 24px 60px; }
  }
</style>
